WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.380
In March 2000, a US index of
technology shares reached its peak.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.940
By October 2002, it had
fallen by about 78 per cent.

3
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.660
Finance is full of people
who are paid to judge risk.

4
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.720
Yet the crash still came.

5
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.650
So if people in finance
are paid to judge risk,

6
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.170
how can a whole market
get it so badly wrong?

7
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.620
In this mission, you'll
see what happens when one

8
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.330
side of a deal knows more than the other.

9
00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.620
Then you'll run a housing
market of your own,

10
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:33.360
and see how far prices can move.

11
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.740
Your mission: find out how
a market full of experts

12
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.770
can still misprice risk.
